WEBVTT

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.110
If there were any way
to restore the old relationship

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.120
that I had with you...

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.040
You were simply marvelous earlier.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.080
Keep up the good work
when you're outside too.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.170
Um, sure, I will.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.630
By the way,

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.630
why were you waiting to ambush me?

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.590
I don't have any ulterior motives.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.850
I thought that we could leave at the same time tomorrow,

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.510
so I came to see you about it.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.850
You did?

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.350
Actually, I had another goal in mind as well.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.860
I also came here to borrow a talented person who might be helpful in my work.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.360
Your work?

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.940
Since Ginshu's been in this state, the misdeeds of the demons have continued to increase.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.320
No matter how many helpers we have,
there are never enough.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.830
Then you're a demon hunter too?

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.330
You might say so.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.080
Then you can see demons too.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.960
Me?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.170
Seriously...

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.090
You hadn't realized that?

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.590
I discarded my eyesight.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.220
That was so I could gain
the power to sense demons.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.100
The price was a bargain.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.100
Y-You went through all that.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.600
Oh? You think it wasn't worth it?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.020
No, that's not what I meant!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:55.110
Of course, I think it's right
to eradicate evil spirits.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.030
Spirits have hearts of humanity and justice,

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.110
allowing them to make distinctions between good and evil.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.660
Is that what you mean?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.330
You really do seem like a tenderhearted boy.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.330
Not particularly.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.870
And oh-so-suspicious along with it.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.380
You seem to be awfully sympathetic
to demons, and kind to them as well.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.220
It all makes me very uneasy.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:24.970
I'm afraid I'm not the sort
to give my trust easily.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:31.190
And so I will continue to keep an eye
on you in the outside world too.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:31.980
Have a good day.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.860
Then I may ask for your help outside.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.490
You know...

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.490
I never thought people were
all that kind to begin with.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:49.000
That's why I think people have to make an effort to be kind and just.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.920
Well, I wonder.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.300
When you look at me with
those sincere eyes of yours,

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.930
it's the only time I feel that I'm being sincere.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.810
Toki, thank you for believing in me.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.940
You're my lucky star.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.280
Recently, I've been remembering his words a lot.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.110
Toki...

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.490
What's the matter with you?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.610
What are you up to?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.120
Sorry, sorry. I was spacing out.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.620
We were told to rest in this room.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.120
Hurry up and come in.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.120
This will warm you up.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.630
What? What happened?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.300
Did the impact mess up your head?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.050
He's probably got bugs
growing in his brain tissue.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.680
Man, I feel better.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.310
You've been under stress recently,
yet you keep trying to look strong.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.810
Those serious expressions
you've been wearing don't suit you.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:00.650
Toki doesn't want you to say that to him.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.190
What the hell do you mean by that?!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.360
You're the one who's been looking gloomy.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.990
Finding fault with other people's expressions is beyond your responsibilities!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.330
Who's gloomy? Who did you call gloomy?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.160
You were about to cry, but the minute
you ate, you were all better.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:13.910
You're a simple creature.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.420
Wh-What the hell?!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.170
Good work.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.130
But I ended up causing more
trouble for you guys.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.260
I'm sorry.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.300
Don't push your luck, idiot.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.770
It's not as if we did all that for your sake.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.140
I was only doing what I wanted to.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:37.850
You've got that right.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.020
The main reason he wants
to stay behind here

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.780
is that it's too much hassle coming and going down that road.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.110
That was very perceptive of you.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.860
You bastard. Do you think I'm stupid?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.620
Does it show?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.030
They've started again.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.580
Right, Toki. Let's leave him
as he is and go to bed.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.290
We've got an early start in the morning.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.750
What? Here?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.630
You don't like the room?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.800
Just deal with it.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.010
They did this for our—

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.470
That's not it.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:13.180
Uh, it's bad in all sorts of ways for boys and girls to sleep in the same room,

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.270
and I think it'd be better if we didn't.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.520
If you want to be alone with him,
then just say so!

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.150
Sorry for bothering you!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.530
No, that's not what I meant!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.030
Let her be. She's just embarrassed.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.030
She's not used to being treated like a girl.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.780
I see.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:36.750
You're pretty much the only one who <i>does</i> treat her like a girl.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:42.250
Shamon treats her like a kid,
and I think of her as a monster.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.300
She <i>is</i> rather hard on you.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.760
Well, since you turned up,
she's changed a little.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.510
Has she become more feminine?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.470
I don't know about that,

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.180
but she still lives her life favoring the practical over the aesthetic.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.520
Don't treat her like a lady too much, though.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.520
If she starts being sexy all of
a sudden, it'll freak me out.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.940
What are you talking about?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.030
A man who can't be nice to women
is a waste of space.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.320
Whatever, you idiot.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.370
Let's get to sleep early tonight.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.030
We'll be busy again tomorrow.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.540
Yeah.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.370
I'll do fine by myself, so don't worry.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.040
Do what you think is best.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.040
Yeah, I'll do that.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.130
I think you should understand,
because I've told you this so many times,

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.880
but be a good kid until I come back, Tokidoki.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:30.880
Yeah.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.220
Listen, this might be the last time we meet,

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.390
so say goodbye like it's the last time.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.100
Yeah!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.100
C'mere!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.600
Suou!

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.100
Toki!

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.110
Okay, Tokidoki, I give up.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.280
That hat's your memento for today.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.700
Take good care of it.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.700
I'll want to use it when I get back,
so don't get it dirty.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.290
Where are you going?

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.250
The usual places: the supermarket,
then the barbershop.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.380
I'll be back a bit late.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.260
See ya!

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.380
It'll be omelet rice for dinner!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.390
Learn to cook something
else for a change, moron!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.600
Shut up, brat!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.390
Moron times three!

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.810
In hindsight, a memento
sounded kind of ominous.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.730
But back then, I just took it for granted.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.200
Then let's be on our way, okay?

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.330
You even kicked me in the face!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.380
All right, I said I'm sorry!

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.920
You think "sorry" is good enough?
And it stunk.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.880
I bet you hadn't even washed your feet.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.340
Hey!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.260
You're noisy, and it's only morning!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.140
Hurry up and make yourselves presentable!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:08:59.930
Huh?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.600
Tsuruume-san, you're wearing a different outfit than usual.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.850
Uh, well, yeah.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:09.110
My usual kimono stands out
a bit too much for going outside.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.070
I don't want to wear this,
but I guess I have to.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.780
Your other kimono's great, really cool,
but this one also suits you.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.950
Wh-What the hell?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.240
Hey, jerk!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.660
If you have something to say too, then just come out and say it!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.460
It's nothing.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.460
Liar!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.960
Toki!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.460
Shinshu-chan!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.300
Good morning.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.960
Your kimono today is cute too.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.840
This is my going-outside kimono.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.720
Does it suit me?

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.720
Yeah, it really suits you.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:40.760
Really?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.890
Yeah.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.220
Everyone...

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.600
Breakfast is ready.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.730
Please come this way.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.230
Sure!

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.730
Shinshu-chan, let's go eat.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.230
Yeah!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.070
Food, food.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.490
Um...

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.320
I'm coming already.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.450
Thanks for the meal.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.540
Huh?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.290
Now that I think of it, where's Ginshu-san?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.830
The sunlight doesn't agree with her health,
so she's sleeping inside.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.960
She apologized for being
unable to see you off

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.800
and said to take good care of Shinshu.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.300
Right.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.510
We'll be leaving as soon as
preparations are complete.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.010
Okay!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.510
I'll follow later and catch up with you.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:23.510
Huh?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.270
I thought you were coming with us.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.270
It's hard for me to keep up
with you young people.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.860
I've sent one of my subordinates
to show you around the town,

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.280
so you needn't worry.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.280
See you later then.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.780
It's no fun getting old, is it, Sasaki-sama?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.330
It's all right.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:48.000
It's the duty of dignitaries
to scold and nag from above.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.790
That seems to suit you very well, Sasaki-sama.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.380
You were picking on some youngsters just yesterday, weren't you?

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:56.880
Eavesdropping is a fine pastime, Kurotobi.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.840
Unfortunately, that's my job.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.840
But that kid talked back to you.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:07.850
He must've been saying things that rather resemble your own pet theory.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.350
Kurotobi, what's your point?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:14.400
If you yap too much,
then you'll lose your tongue.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.900
My, how terrifying.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.360
Well, I have a report from the town.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:26.120
A guy with an unusual appearance was seen accompanying a townsman to Nihonbashi.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.370
Who is it?

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.420
Judging from the aura, it seems that one of them might be a demon.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.380
Go after it.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.050
Orders understood, sir.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.340
Somebody fixed the hanging blinds.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.840
Now they're back to how they were before.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.850
See you, then. Look after yourself.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.180
Shinonome,

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.180
hold out your hand.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.230
O-Ow!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.940
What the hell are you doing?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.900
Here you go.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:11:59.690
Look after it for me.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.660
When I part ways with someone,
I always make a big deal of it.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.160
I'll come back, so you can
return it to me then.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.540
I promise.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.660
You're <i>really</i> making a big deal of it.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.210
It's my "jinx."

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.670
I have to do it.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.460
Aw, man.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.880
All right, hold out your hand.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:19.670
Shinonome?

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.510
Here.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.100
Don't take too long returning it.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.180
Sure.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.560
They have gone.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.690
How is your health?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.070
It is fine.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:42.570
Besides, this might be the last time
I set eyes on them.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.070
Why did you choose to stay behind here?

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:49.580
I'm not supposed to say this myself,

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.580
but you seem to be the one withholding
the most information at the moment.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.080
I'd like to hear it.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.080
I see.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:00.170
What would you like to know?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.090
Right now, only you and I are here.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.470
I do not mind answering you.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.130
In that case, first,

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:09.430
why didn't you tell him to lift
your curse from the outset?

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.730
Shouldn't that have come
<i>before</i> asking him for help?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.350
I have another question as well.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.690
If you can really see the future of this world,
how much do you know?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.690
You know who this Teiten really is, don't you?

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:27.200
The gods alone are party
to Teiten's true identity.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.700
Though Bonten would...

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.780
No...

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:33.750
If it were Kokuten, the closest existence to Teiten, then possibly...

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.210
I thought Kokuten's identity
wasn't actually known.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.590
You know better than I, do you not?

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.090
Kokuten is Yakou.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:44.590
Him?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:48.090
It is kept confidential to avoid spreading panic among the people.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.310
So Teiten is in league with the demons.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.930
No. Yakou is an enemy to the demons as well.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.400
Yakou drives demons mad,

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.810
drives people mad,

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.820
drives the world itself mad.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:07.320
And if such a thing is closest to Teiten...

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:13.740
It means that this world, Amatsuki, might be driven to madness by its own creator's intent.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.710
If I were to attempt to foil that plan,

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.670
Teiten would not even let me try,

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.960
and even the Blank Page
could not save my life.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:30.470
He went to try and lift
the deadly curse on you.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.970
Doesn't he have the power
to alter heaven's net?

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.640
Perhaps you will understand
if I rephrase myself.

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:40.690
This curse upon me isn't a curse
that will lead to my death.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.730
It is a curse that keeps me from dying.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:49.610
Give me your soul!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.410
Well, purification completed
for the seventh monster.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.160
What just happened then?

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.500
Why did the box suddenly break in half?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.840
It must be nice not being
able to see it, really.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.090
It's all right.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.840
Most parts of the premises
have been purified.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.560
Oh? It's morning already, is it?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:16.930
Sorry to keep you all night.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:17.850
No, no.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.480
I suggested it in the first place.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:24.440
I admit I didn't expect it to
take quite this long, but...

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.610
It seems strange though.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:31.570
These buildings aren't derelict, yet so many spirits have gathered at this one house.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:35.830
These peculiar sounds have started to be heard only recently,

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.120
but it's ominous how, day by day,
matters grow worse.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:42.040
And then yesterday...

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.380
What's going on here?

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.380
It came from the storehouse.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:00.770
The storeroom always has a water tank in it to keep it humid.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:03.600
It should've been impossible for even a spark to occur in there.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:07.270
Something must be in that storehouse.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.490
I searched in there first,

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.410
and I couldn't find even one evil presence.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.410
It looks as though ordinary
methods won't work here.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.910
Would you mind if I took a short rest?

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.920
Of course not.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.130
In that case, I'll go prepare for breakfast.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.630
On the contrary, that storehouse is brimming with a noble aura.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.970
It practically feels like the grounds of a shrine.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.400
Tonight.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.820
I shall finally come to you tonight...

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.370
to take you back.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.120
Hey, Gen-san,

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.580
I brought the goods you ordered.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.750
Somebody!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:09.750
You should not have remained behind.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.010
It pains my heart that you have been caught up in all this.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.340
I was being somewhat naive,

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:20.010
and that is why I made such a request of him.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.730
But he said of his own accord that he would lift my curse,

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.810
and since Shinshu has now left the shrine,

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.150
this must be the right course after all.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:36.320
I must take the course that I believe in

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.490
and keep those who must
be protected from harm.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.120
The name "Ginshu" carries that responsibility.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.080
Good night.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.580
I am glad you were here to listen to me.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.960
Oh, no...

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.840
I wanted someone to know.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.590
Or do I just feel that way
due to lingering regrets?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.850
This life was gone long ago.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.470
Why should I regret it?

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:07.020
And despite all of that,
will you again shed tears...

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.150
Bonten?

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:15.570
I won't let you be the only one
to be freed from a curse...

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.200
Ginshu.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.450
Please wait here until the master arrives.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.080
Man, this mansion is huge.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.580
Whose house is this?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.420
It's useless to think about that.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.300
After all, this place isn't part
of the human world.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:37.840
Isn't it obvious after seeing that Nue and the child just now

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.350
that you've stumbled into
a pretty dangerous place?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:42.600
A Nue?

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.810
What's that?

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.980
Wh-What is it?

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.020
If you want to say something,
tell me straight.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:49.850
You're blockheaded,

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:50.350
simple,

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.100
and oblivious.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.610
You do things without thinking
about the consequences.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.730
You're sure to end up dead
by the side of the road somewhere.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.070
Wh-What did you say <i>that</i> for?!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.160
You're the one who told me to!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.490
If you want to argue, then bring it on.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:08.580
No, even I can kind of see that it's true.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:11.330
Besides, you're not a normal human, are you?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.750
How long have you known?

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.460
From the start, of course!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:20.260
It'd be pretty strange if I thought you were normal,
given that weird getup of yours.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.260
I guess.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:28.270
I'm sorry to say, but when it comes to weirdos, I know a few already.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.400
In the first place, when you fell on top of me,

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.110
I thought you were a bit strange.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.690
You look around the same age as me,

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:40.360
but you're as light as a baby.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.780
Despite that, you have superhuman strength, and you're remarkably agile.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:46.330
I couldn't possibly think
you were human after that.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.370
So why didn't you run away?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.080
Well...

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.040
I would've run away if you had done anything outrageous to me,

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:58.050
but you treated my wounds,
and you seemed to be having difficulties.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.300
Is that all?

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.800
Sure.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:05.800
You've had people run off and leave you with the bill before, haven't you?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.430
Are you really this idiotic?

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.850
How can you bring yourself
to accompany a stranger?

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.310
Don't you have any sense of caution?

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.520
It's okay.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.280
If you did something bad to me,

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.530
then it'd be my own fault for being a poor judge of character.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.530
As a native of Edo,

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.910
I'm prepared for the worst!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:32.330
Edo has long been a gathering
place for vagabonds.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.000
Asking people about their pasts
and backgrounds just isn't done.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:39.130
People can get on pretty well without knowing stuff like that about each other.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.970
Weirdo.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.720
By the way, I don't think
I introduced myself earlier.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.600
I'm called Heihachi.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.470
Nice to meet you.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.350
I'm Tsuyukusa.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.230
You didn't have to be nice.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.900
I apologize for keeping you waiting.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.400
I am afraid the master has some business to take care of.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.900
Please forgive the discourtesy.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.740
This smell...

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.160
It's human blood, isn't it?

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:08.120
Is Yakou's madness so powerful?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.370
Have you forgotten that the flesh and blood of humans is poison?!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.370
Why are you getting so agitated?

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:19.460
Is it your job to kill human beings?

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.880
Have you fallen so far, Inari?!

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.470
You were the one who refused my plea for help.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:31.520
You do not have any right to complain if I ask someone else for assistance.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:32.600
No,

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:35.850
I hold no grudge.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.650
I am merely glad that you came to me.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.480
By the way,

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.730
why is there a human here?

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:43.740
I...

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:44.570
You just—

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:47.910
Heihachi!
